WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.234
-Ray Romano. Welcome back.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.200
Congrats on the movie.
I'm very excited.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.000
It's nice to see you. You look
good. How have you been?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.667
-I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:13.100
I actually --
I just got over COVID.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.834
I hadn't had it.
I assume...?

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.400
-Yeah, I did. Yeah.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.734
-I got it about --
about a month ago.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:22.501
-I'm happy you're fine.
-Oh, it was fine.

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:25.601
Yeah, it was bad timing,
actually, when I got it

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.701
because it was
my wife's birthday.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.868
My wife.
You met my wife backstage.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:31.067
-Beautiful. Yeah.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.467
-Yeah, she was turning 60.
-Is that right?

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.634
-So we had a big party planned.
We came into New York.

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:39.834
And we had a restaurant
rented out with friends,

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:43.701
families, and relatives,
and then I got COVID.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:46.300
And so two days later,
the party.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.767
And she was -- We have
an apartment in New York.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.834
She was walking
through the elevator.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:55.300
And this will tell you
how long we've been married.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.467
-Yeah.
-I waved to her.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.267
I was in my pajamas,
you know, and I just waved.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.234
I said, "Happy birthday,"
you know.

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:04.000
And she just looked at me.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.734
I thought I would get,
"We're going to miss you,"

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.767
or, "Hope you feel okay."

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.968
-Yeah.
-And I got this.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:15.467
"I feel like punching you."

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:18.133
Not kidding. Not kidding.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.667
-"I feel like punching you."
-Yes, 'cause she thought --

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:21.834
-Yeah, and now she's gotta go --

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.934
-She blamed me
for the COVID 'cause...

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.868
'Cause she probably knew
deep down

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:29.133
there was a little bit of me
that was kind of happy.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:30.968
-Happy to be home.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.033
You're in pajamas.
You're hanging out at home.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.200
-But it's not true.
It's not true.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.367
-Yeah, but it wasn't --
It wasn't that bad, though, huh?

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:40.901
-No, no, it wasn't bad.
I'm happy. I'm good. I'm glad.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:44.200
I'm glad the numbers are down.
I can't --

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.534
I dread if we ever
have to do lockdown again.

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.334
How was lockdown for you?
-Oh, it was terrible.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.868
It was tough.
-Because you have two --

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:51.167
-I have two little girls.
Yeah.

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:52.934
-Okay, I have four children
who are grown

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:56.934
and out of the house
who came back for COVID.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.434
They came back.
Yeah, I have --

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.868
My daughter's the oldest.
I have three boys.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:04.267
They came back. A year
and a half back in the house.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.033
And when they left...
-Man: Ooh!

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:09.267
-Yes, I learned something
about my kids when they left.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.734
My order of favorites
has changed.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.267
Yes.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:17.033
No. I thought it was locked in.

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:20.100
You think it's for life.
But they --

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.501
Four is still four.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.300
Because he's horrible.
That kid's horrible.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.534
He's not going away.
No, he's not going anywhere.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.033
But I did a 1-and-3.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:31.000
1 and 3 did a flip on me.
-1 and 3.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.300
-Yes, and for
a number of reasons.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.234
But the main one was --
During COVID --

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:40.434
Now, I was at the
kitchen table with number 3.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.000
It was me and number 3.
Yeah. Greg.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.467
Me and Greg.
We gave him a name. Greg.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:46.734
-That's nice of you.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.234
-He has a name.
-That's nice of you.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.234
-And so it was me and Greg.
And my wife was in the bathroom.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:53.701
And all of a sudden she starts
yelling from the bathroom,

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.701
you know, "Who was just in
here?! Who was in here?

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.067
There's pee all over the floor."

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.501
Yeah. Oh, yeah. She was mad.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:04.367
And Greg looked at me
and he could see the guilt.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.400
He could see the guilt
in my eyes.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.801
Yes.

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:09.667
And she's like,
"Who was in here?"

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.234
And I didn't even --
I didn't ask Greg to do this,

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.467
but he just looked
to the bathroom and he went,

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.767
"It was me, Mom."
He took a bullet for me.

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:18.467
-Wow.
-Yes.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:20.167
-Wow.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.234
-That's number 1.
-Now he's number 1.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:24.634
Moved him to number 1.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.734
-That's automatic.
That's automatic number 1.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.200
-He jumped on a grenade
for you.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.868
-Yes, exactly.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:32.267
So we have a new number 1.
I'm sorry, Ali.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.200
Sorry, my daughter.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.033
My daughter's been number 1
since the day she was born.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.767
-But she wasn't
going to do that for you.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.901
-No, no.
She's smarter than the boys.

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.300
And she works harder
than the boys.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.834
But, yeah,
she wouldn't have done that.

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.634
She wouldn't have done that.
Well, she could --

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:48.467
Technically, she couldn't
have convinced my wife...

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.934
Yes.
By the way -- By the way --

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.701
Yes, my wife, she knew.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:58.667
My wife knew it was a male
who got pee

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.501
"all over the floor."

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:04.133
I'm telling you.
I went in there. Three drops.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:07.267
It was three drops at the most,
which you have --

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:11.467
Ladies, you have to give us
three drops. We get three drops.

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:12.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:16.634
That's the law --
That's physics. That's the --

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:18.634
But you know what I'm saying.
That's the law of bounce.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.167
It's the law of bounce.

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:24.434
-Yeah. You've been married --
You've been married a long time.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:25.834
-I have been married
a long time.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.834
I won't even -- I don't even
want to say the number.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:32.067
It's -- I'll give you --
I'll give you an example

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.033
of how long I've been married.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.634
If the "I want to punch you"
is not a good enough example...

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:39.367
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-...here's a better one.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.601
My son came over for dinner.
Him and his girlfriend.

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:46.901
Matt. My son.
Number 2. Number 2.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.000
He could be 1.
He's got potential.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.701
-Okay. Okay.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.634
-Yeah. He's got potential.
He's got a --

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:54.601
He's got a ponytail that's
holding him back right now.

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:56.801
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:56.801 --> 00:04:58.334
[ Cymbals crash ]
I can't. I can't.

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:01.367
Sorry, guys. Anybody up there
with a ponytail?

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.601
I can't make -- Number 1
can't have a ponytail.

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:06.334
No, but --

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:08.100
But he came over
with his girlfriend.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.200
And it was very nice. It was us.
We were having dinner.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.400
It was in, you know --
at our house.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.534
And in the middle of it,
I get a text, and I look down,

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:19.567
and it's from my wife,
who's right there.

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:21.400
She's sitting
right in front of me.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.067
Yeah. And it's just two words.
"Chewing loud."

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.567
Yes.

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:29.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:32.567
Yes. That's right.
At first I thought

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:35.667
she was talking about
the girlfriend, you know?

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.501
And I was like,
"Oh. We're gonna trash?

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:41.834
Alright. That's great. Yeah."

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.501
"Yeah, you're right.

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:45.234
She's a horse.
What's she doing?"

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:48.067
-Yeah, exactly.
-But 35 years, actually.

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:50.067
-35 years.
-35 years married.

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:51.133
-Yeah.
-Ray!

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:52.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:05:52.834 --> 00:05:55.534
-Ray, 35 years married.
-How long you?

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:57.567
-18.
-18 for you?

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:59.100
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.901
-You're half. You're half.
Almost half.

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:02.400
-Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.667
-It will change.

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.634
But things will change
in the second half.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:08.334
It's great. I'm not complaining.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.000
I have a great wife.
I have a great marriage.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.167
But things --
things are different.

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:16.601
When we have --
When we have sex now,

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:20.100
my wife actually
has to take off her Apple Watch

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.501
'cause it keeps saying,
"Time to move. Time to move."

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:28.801
"Have you...

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:33.767
Have you fallen?
Have you fallen?

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:37.801
Your pulse rate is too low.
Your pulse rate is too low."

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.300
-"Did you fall?"
-That deserved a thing.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.934
-Yeah, that deserves
a rim shot there.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:46.467
I want to talk about --
-Oh, my gosh. "Did you fall?"

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:48.234
Can we talk about your film?

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.267
Your new film.
"Somewhere in Queens."

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:51.868
-Yes.
-This is a big deal.

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:53.767
You co-wrote it. You star in it.

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:55.334
And this is your
first time ever directing.

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:57.334
-I did, yeah.
-Ray Romano!

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:59.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:02.367
-And you're getting
great reviews.

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:05.934
But what is the inspiration
behind this film?

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:08.367
-Well, it's based on what
I was going through in my life.

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:11.300
My son, my youngest son --
six foot.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.701
He's 6'5".

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.534
I don't know
if you ever met him. Joe.

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.767
And he played on the
high-school basketball team,

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:19.234
and I would go to the game.

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:22.901
It was so exciting to have a kid
who was a star of basketball.

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:25.100
But we knew he wasn't
going to play in college.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:29.167
So the last game I went to,
I went down on the court,

00:07:29.167 --> 00:07:31.067
I hugged the coach,
and I got emotional

00:07:31.067 --> 00:07:34.934
because I was going to
miss this with my son.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:36.634
And if I'm being honest,

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.767
I was going to miss
being the father,

00:07:38.767 --> 00:07:40.601
you know, getting the attention.

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:43.434
It's pathetic.
How sad. It's so sad.

00:07:43.434 --> 00:07:45.634
I don't get enough attention.

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:49.534
You know, I'm on TV or whatever.
I got to get more attention.

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:52.100
Right, right.
But I just -- I just thought,

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.968
what if that was a guy,
a poor guy

00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:55.601
who that's all he had
in his life?

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:59.267
He felt very small, you know,
this working-class guy.

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:00.601
And that's all he had.

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:02.000
He lived vicariously
through his son.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.434
So that was the origin
of the story.

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:07.267
And my agent convinced me
to direct it.

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:08.567
I didn't want to direct it,

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:11.133
but he said it was
too personal a story.

00:08:11.133 --> 00:08:12.434
-But it worked. It's fantastic.

00:08:12.434 --> 00:08:14.100
-Oh, yeah, it scared the hell
out of me, but I did it.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.934
-You did it, buddy.
It's unbelievable. It's great.

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:17.667
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:08:17.667 --> 00:08:20.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:22.367
-I want to show a clip.

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:24.267
Do you want --
Do you want to set the clip up?

00:08:24.267 --> 00:08:26.501
-The clip is when my --
So, my son

00:08:26.501 --> 00:08:28.968
is a introverted kid
who doesn't say much.

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:30.834
He's shy.
He's never had a girlfriend.

00:08:30.834 --> 00:08:32.868
And after the game,
we're meeting this girl

00:08:32.868 --> 00:08:35.200
for the first time with my wife,

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.434
who is a typical overprotective
Italian mother.

00:08:38.434 --> 00:08:39.868
And this is it.
-There you go.

00:08:39.868 --> 00:08:41.868
-Here's Ray Romano
in "Somewhere in Queens."

00:08:41.868 --> 00:08:43.601
Check it out.

00:08:43.601 --> 00:08:45.567
-It was really nice
to finally meet you guys,

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:46.968
no thanks to this one.

00:08:46.968 --> 00:08:48.701
[ Chuckles ] Bye.

00:08:50.267 --> 00:08:52.601
[ Chuckles ]
Wait. Come here.

00:08:52.601 --> 00:08:55.167
-Oh.
-Okay. Go.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:58.100
-Come to dinner Sunday!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.100
-Ma, she --
-I would love to.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.734
I love Italian food.

00:09:01.734 --> 00:09:03.968
-Okay. Sunday. 12:00.

00:09:03.968 --> 00:09:08.133
-Dinner at 12:00. I love it.
I'll be there. Thank you.

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:11.834
Now take me to work, boy!
You want me to get fired?

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:13.667
Wait. I'm slipping.

00:09:13.667 --> 00:09:15.334
-Kind of heavy.
-Hey!

00:09:15.334 --> 00:09:17.534
-Sorry.

00:09:17.534 --> 00:09:19.701
-Do not [bleep] like her.

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:21.701
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:23.367
-Excellent delivery right there.

00:09:23.367 --> 00:09:25.400
Ray Romano, everybody.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.667
"Somewhere in Queens"
opens in theaters tomorrow.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:31.834
Congratulations, buddy.
Apple Watch. That's the best.

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:34.434
Zoe Lister-Jones
joins us after the break.

00:09:34.434 --> 00:09:35.801
Stick around, everybody.

